WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.833
- [Instructor] In this video,

00:00:01.833 --> 00:00:05.310
I'm going to talk about a unit
of length known as the meter,

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.760
which you might have heard of before.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.210
It's really probably the
most used unit of length

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.410
in the world.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:16.930
And so the natural question
is how long is a meter?

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.290
Well, one way to get a
rough sense of a meter

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.160
is imagine a reasonably
tall basketball player.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.510
So a good bit taller
than your average man.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:28.290
So a good bit taller than
me, I'm about average height.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.780
So that's your basketball player there.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.113
He's got his basketball.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.530
He might be roughly two meters tall.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.960
So this would be two meters,

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.170
one meter, and this lowercase
m is short for meter.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.400
And then two meters.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.520
Another way to think about a meter

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.330
is if you took a long step,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.060
if you're, let's say,
seven or eight years old,

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.640
and if you were to take a long step,

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.180
you might travel about a meter.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.680
So that's your long step,

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.320
right over there.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:08.050
It might be close to a meter, roughly,

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.170
it's not necessarily going
to be exactly a meter,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.480
but it might be close.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.480
Now a related unit of length
is known as the centimeter,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.850
and you might already recognize

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.180
that it has the word meter in it,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.630
and it also has the word centi.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:30.592
Now you might already
know that the word cent,

00:01:30.592 --> 00:01:32.660
100 cents make $1.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:36.000
You might know the word
century, that's 100 years.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.390
So you might say, is this 100 meters?

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.560
You'd be kind of close,
but kind of far off.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.670
It's not 100 meters, it's
not bigger than a meter.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.370
It's actually a lot smaller than a meter.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:50.950
A centimeter, 100 of them
will equal one meter.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.990
So one way to think about it
is if I write it in shorthand

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.410
100 and you normally write
it as lowercase c and m.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:02.310
So 100 centimeters are equal to one meter.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.910
So on these pictures right over here,

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:09.910
a centimeter would be much
smaller than a meter right over,

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.550
even what I just drew there

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.760
would be a lot less than a centimeter.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.970
And one way to think about a centimeter,

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:18.610
it might be if you stick your finger out,

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.860
your finger, depending on
how large your finger is,

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.470
might be about a centimeter wide.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:28.680
As a grown average-sized man,

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.510
my finger is actually
about two centimeters wide.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.360
If I take my index finger
and if I were to measure it,

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.740
I would approximate it
as about two centimeters.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:42.380
So 100 centimeters make up a meter,

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.850
which hopefully makes a
little bit of sense to you.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.480
Now given what we've just learned

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.870
about meters and centimeters,

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.110
let's think about what is
better to measure with,

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.290
depending on the size of the thing.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:59.290
So if I was looking at a let's
say fairly tall of some kind,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.260
what would I wanna measure that with?

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.870
Would I be more likely
to measure that in meters

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.660
or would I be more likely to measure that

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.830
in the centimeters?

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.730
Pause this video and think about that.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.200
Well, a fairly tall tree
is going to be a lot taller

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.160
than even this basketball player,

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.520
so normally, people are likely
to measure this in meters.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:24.700
A reasonably tall tree could
be 10 meters or 20 meters,

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.560
or even in certain cases
30 meters or taller.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.560
Now what if I were instead
measuring the length of a mouse,

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:39.210
so my best drawing of a mouse
here, draw its little paws,

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.910
kind of looks like a fish with a tail.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.620
But let's say that this is a mouse,

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.610
would I measure this in
meters or centimeters?

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:50.610
Well, a mouse is much smaller
in length than a tree is tall,

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:54.743
so you would likely measure
this in centimeters.

00:03:56.308 --> 00:04:01.308
A small mouse might be
maybe five or 10 centimeters

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.600
in length, right over here.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.710
Now let's compare another way

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.600
or decide another way to think about

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.560
whether we're measuring
in centimeters or meters.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.297
Let's say that I went
to the local gymnasium,

00:04:17.462 --> 00:04:19.490
and there's a pool there.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.150
There's a pool, that's
the water in the pool.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.520
And I were to measure the length.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.380
And I know it is 25-something,

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:31.320
it's either 25 meters or 25 centimeters.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.500
Remember, this is the pool at the gym.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.333
Pause this video,

00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:37.963
do you think this would be
25 centimeters or 25 meters?

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.950
Well, as you can imagine,
the length of a pool,

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.380
this tall basketball player,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.760
many of them could lie down and to end

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.530
to get to this length of this pool.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.600
So this would be a 25 meter pool.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.903
A 25 centimeter pool,

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:57.370
that would actually probably be

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:59.218
about the size of a cell phone

00:04:59.218 --> 00:05:01.330
or maybe smaller or a little bit larger,

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.600
depending on the cell phone
that you're talking about.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.420
So for a pool, you'd be
talking in terms of meters.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:12.050
What if we had a building of some kind,

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.823
so this is a building right over here,

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:19.770
and let's say it is a
four storey building.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:26.380
And someone were to say that
it is 15 something tall,

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:30.093
would this be 15 meters
tall or 15 centimeters tall?

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.960
Well, 15 centimeters, that
might be a Lego building.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.243
A real building would be
15 meters in this scenario.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:43.170
Now what if I were to say
the length of my thumb,

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.870
the length of my thumb, right over here.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.690
And I know it is five-something,

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:55.810
this length right over
here, it is five-something,

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.670
it's either five meters
or five centimeters,

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.750
which one do you think it is?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.220
Well, if it was five meters,

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:03.860
I would be a very, very, very large giant.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:08.610
My thumb would be twice as
tall or more than twice as tall

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.620
as a fairly tall basketball player.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:15.080
So this would be five
centimeters right over here.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.590
So hopefully that gives you a sense

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:18.320
of meters and centimeters.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.410
And on Khan Academy,
there's a lot more practice.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.740
So you can get a little bit more sense

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:23.690
of estimating with
these, or thinking about

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:27.353
when one unit or the
other is more appropriate.

